  "id": "COMPOUND:19466 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Catiguanin B is shown to have a target relationship with DNA polymerase iota, as evidenced by its interaction with hepatocytes and VMRC-LCP, which in turn targets DNA polymerase iota. The evidence suggests that Catiguanin B may act on a common downstream target, DNA polymerase iota, through a pathway involving VMRC-LCP. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with some variation in the strength of the evidence across the different paths. The mechanism appears to involve a series of molecular interactions where Catiguanin B may inhibit DNA polymerase iota through a target-mediated pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of VMRC-LCP. The integration of these paths suggests a potential role for Catiguanin B in regulating DNA polymerase iota activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and the extent of its biological impact.",
